          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+spaces"} complex analytic spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group"} multiplicative group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_m
            classifies non-vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+functions"} holomorphic functions
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}_m
            classifies
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundles"} holomorphic line bundles
            %em holomorphic line 2-bundle
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{G}_m
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+2-bundle"} principal 2-bundle
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}_m
          %p
            This means that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of holomorphic line 2-bundles on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+space"} complex analytic space
            or more generally on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} complex analytic ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+stack"} Brauer stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Br
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Br}(X) \coloneqq [X,\mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}_m]
            (the line 2-bundle itself is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} associated ∞-bundle
            to the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}\mathbb{G}_m
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
            of a given map
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔾
                      %mi m
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}^2 \mathbb{G}_m
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of holomorphic line 2-bundles form the elements of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bigger+Brauer+group"} bigger Brauer group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+group"} Brauer group
            proper if they are torsion).
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
            includes (
            %a{:href => "#Chatterjee98"}> Chatterjee 98
            ,
            %a{:href => "#Brylinski00"} Brylinski 00
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#MathaiStevenson02"} Mathai-Stevenson 02, section 7
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#dixmierdouady_class Dixmier-Douady class
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dixmier-Douady+class"} Dixmier-Douady class
            of holomorphic line 2-bundles, hence the higher analog of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphism"} connecting homomorphism
            on degee 2 of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+in+cohomology"} long exact sequence in cohomology
            which is induced by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+exact+sequence"} exponential exact sequence
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+geometry"} complex analytic geometry
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi DD
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  DD\;\colon\;  H^2(-,\mathbb{G}_m) \longrightarrow H^3(-,\mathbb{Z})
                  \\,.
          %h3#RelationToHigherTwistorTransforms Relation to higher twistor transforms
          %p
            Holomorphic line 2-bundles appear in the higher degree analogs of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+transforms"} twistor transforms
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Chatterjee98"} Chatterjee 98
            %a{:href => "twistor%20space#ReferencesApplicationToSelfDual2FormField"} twistor – References – Application to self-dual 2-forms
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+complex+analytic+geometry"} higher complex analytic geometry
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+n-bundle"} holomorphic line n-bundle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+line+2-bundle"} algebraic line 2-bundle
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Discussion in relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson+regulators"} Beilinson regulators
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Brylinski94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Holomorphic gerbes and the Beilinson regulator
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Brylinski94.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Early discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbes"} bundle gerbes
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Chatterjee98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Chatterjee"}> David Chatterjee
              , section 5 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Gerbs
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://people.maths.ox.ac.uk/hitchin/hitchinstudents/chatterjee.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion with an eye towards of holomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#MathaiStevenson02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varghese+Mathai"}> Varghese Mathai
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chern character in twisted K-theory: equivariant and holomorphic cases
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://lanl.arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0201010v5"} arXiv:hep-th/0201010v5
          %p An equivariant example arising from more algebro-geometric origin is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Felder"}> Giovanni Felder
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andre+Henriques"} Andre Henriques
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chenchang+Zhu"} Chenchang Zhu
              = succeed "," do
                %em A gerbe for the elliptic gamma function
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0601337"} arXiv:math/0601337
              (
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1215/S0012-7094-08-14111-0"}> doi
              )
          %p
            Discussion connecting explicitly to the holomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brauer+group"} Brauer group
            includes
          %ul
            %li#BenBassat08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oren+Ben-Bassat"}> Oren Ben-Bassat
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gerbes and the Holomorphic Brauer Group of Complex Tori
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0811.2746"} arXiv:0811.2746
            %li
              %p
                Edoardo Ballico,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oren+Ben-Bassat"} Oren Ben-Bassat
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Meromorphic Line Bundles and Holomorphic Gerbes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1101.2216"} arXiv:1101.2216
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#BenBassat11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oren+Ben-Bassat"}> Oren Ben-Bassat
              ,
              %em Equivariant Gerbes on Complex Tori
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1102.2312"}> arXiv:1102.2312
              )
          %h3#ReferencesOnReductiveGroup Basic line 2-bundles on reductive groups
          %p
            The existence of the “basic” 2-line bundle (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+line+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons line 3-bundle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reductive+group"} reductive group
            (such as
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SL(n,\mathbb{C})
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              , around theorem 5.4.10 (p. 226-227) of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Loop spaces and characteristic classes
          %p The actual construction appears in
          %ul
            %li#Brylinski00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean-Luc+Brylinski"}> Jean-Luc Brylinski
              ,
              %em Gerbes on complex reductive Lie groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0002158"}> arXiv:math/0002158
              )
